      "content": "It sounds like you are going through an incredibly painful and disorienting time. The silence after a loss can feel deafening, and it's completely understandable that you feel lost when your daily routines have been so fundamentally altered. Please know that these intense feelings of emptiness are a normal part of grief, and you don't have to navigate this overwhelming void alone. Reaching out to a grief counselor or a support group can provide a safe space to process these complicated emotions.",
